{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785012118,"nonce":"3pXD54VJf+Aj6tbNEPGkCQs1bmM=","message":"Fixed on integrate/open-issues-2026-07-26 (45e608c, 192a44d).\n\nThe harvest no longer gates on exit == 0: it is owed for any terminated step until the index annotation lands on the Pod, so drive_workspace harvests before touching egress-done. Rather than adding a second barrier, this reuses the one #78 introduced — settled_state reports Running for Failed{class: Step} while the index is still outstanding. Deliberately narrower than the Succeeded withhold: a failed step`s workspace is not an output, so a wedged sidecar cannot hide a verdict already known. Infra/Timeout/Config/Lost pass through verbatim.\n\nA harvest error is logged as evidence and returned as DriveErr::Transient only, never OutputContract/InputMissing, so it can never surface as Failed{Config}/Failed{Infra}. The class is re-derived from the Pod exit code each poll, so a broken harvest can delay the report but never change it; re-harvest is idempotent (same object keys), bounded by the step-timeout backstop.\n\nVerified LIVE against the kind cluster, not just in unit tests:\n  cluster::artifacts_are_harvested_from_a_failed_step  PASS (15.3s)\n  full kind tier 16/16 PASS, including cancel / sleeping-step-deadline / rerun-supersede, which all traverse the modified settled_state.\nWorkspace suite 656/656 green.","files":null}]}